// TEST: Tuple Destructure Width Mismatch (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3999
// ERROR-CONTAINS: but the value is a 2-tuple
// ============================================================================
// A destructuring `let` whose name count matches NEITHER the value's
// top-level width NOR its flattened leaf count. Every one of the four
// destructuring sites used to fall back to the structural list and let fresh
// inference variables cover the overflow ("Fall back to structural, let fresh
// vars handle overflow") -- MEASURED consequence: `blade check` said OK and
// g++ then rejected `std::get<2>` applied to a `std::tuple<double, double>`.
//
// `tupleDestructureArityError` is shared by all four (DeclLet, `let static`,
// block `StmtLet`, expression position) so they cannot drift, and stands down
// for every non-tuple scrutinee -- a `Poly` pack or a still-unresolved type is
// somebody else's judgement, and answering here would turn inference order
// into a diagnostic.
//
// The bare-comma binder (`021`) inherits this for free: it produces the same
// `PatTuple` the parenthesized form does.
// ============================================================================
let t = 1.0, 2.0
let a, b, c = t
let s = a + b + c
// EXPECT: typecheck failure -- three names against a 2-tuple
